; expect 0
; A spine supplying MORE arguments than the callee declares. `adder`
; takes one parameter and returns a closure, so the surplus argument
; belongs to that closure. Flattening the whole spine into one direct
; call passed both to `adder` and answered with the returned closure's
; ADDRESS. Every function value absorbs exactly one argument per call.
(fn (adder n) (lambda (x) x))
(fn (main) (if (== ((adder 10) 5) 5) 0 1))
